                <pb facs="0167" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/4616: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Personal Representative of the President</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-15T14:00:00-05:00">January 15, 1934—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 2:55 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. My telegram No. 21, January 15, 1 p.m. Revolutionary junta has decided to
                    support Hevia for the Presidency. Hevia has secured (I hear) a written promise
                    of support from Mendieta.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
